WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.096 --> 00:00:01.663
- You smell nice.

00:00:01.663 --> 00:00:02.496
- You too.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:04.519
- Yeah I know.

00:00:04.519 --> 00:00:06.852
(pop music)

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.538
- Hi my name is Kramer Cruz.

00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:13.657
- Hello my name is Kara Anthony.

00:00:13.657 --> 00:00:15.247
- We had been together for about a year,

00:00:15.247 --> 00:00:16.211
just over a year.

00:00:16.211 --> 00:00:18.025
And as the relationship got more serious

00:00:18.025 --> 00:00:20.158
obviously she wanted
more and more commitment.

00:00:20.158 --> 00:00:22.600
I just wasn't really ready to do that.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.404
- When I signed up for this
and decided to do this game,

00:00:26.404 --> 00:00:28.639
I thought, oh it'll be fine,

00:00:28.639 --> 00:00:32.225
we're still cool, we could work together.

00:00:32.225 --> 00:00:36.406
But actually the anxiety that
has come about doing this

00:00:36.406 --> 00:00:39.547
today is a little overwhelming,
it's a little somber.

00:00:39.547 --> 00:00:41.245
- Hey my name is Quinn Knox.

00:00:41.245 --> 00:00:42.383
- Hi I'm Leo Valez.

00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:44.792
- We dated for I guess about six months.

00:00:44.792 --> 00:00:46.571
Things got a little too comfortable

00:00:46.571 --> 00:00:49.932
and we just decided that it was best

00:00:49.932 --> 00:00:51.534
not to see each other anymore.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.305
- We were very mature about it,

00:00:53.305 --> 00:00:56.299
so we talked it out, and
we tried to make it work.

00:00:56.299 --> 00:00:58.755
But once the fire is
gone, it's kind of hard

00:00:58.755 --> 00:01:00.013
to reignite it, and that's something that

00:01:00.013 --> 00:01:01.220
I think should come naturally.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.651
I hope to at least keep him in my life

00:01:02.651 --> 00:01:03.933
because Quinn's a great guy.

00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:07.173
To have him involved
would be a great thing,

00:01:07.173 --> 00:01:08.264
he's someone I really value.

00:01:08.264 --> 00:01:12.097
- I don't understand
exactly why it broke off.

00:01:12.947 --> 00:01:14.258
I don't think he does either,

00:01:14.258 --> 00:01:17.008
but I'm open for new experiences.

00:01:20.097 --> 00:01:20.942
- [Leo] It's all coming back to me now.

00:01:20.942 --> 00:01:22.004
- [Quinn] Okay we can
just leave your shoes.

00:01:22.004 --> 00:01:23.171
I'm like, OCD.

00:01:27.298 --> 00:01:28.196
- [Leo] Conservative start.

00:01:28.196 --> 00:01:30.683
(laughter)

00:01:30.683 --> 00:01:33.684
- [Kramer] Oh, okay good that's easy.

00:01:33.684 --> 00:01:34.517
Oh.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.131
- [Leo] Oh no.

00:01:40.882 --> 00:01:41.715
Spiderman!

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:46.448
- Do I have to keep this one up?

00:01:46.448 --> 00:01:49.130
(laughter)

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.713
I'll push you over.

00:01:56.463 --> 00:01:58.745
- [Leo] Yeah that's the rule of the,

00:01:58.745 --> 00:01:59.935
(laughter)

00:01:59.935 --> 00:02:01.408
- I feel like I'm doing yoga.

00:02:01.408 --> 00:02:02.657
- [Quinn] You're inching away from me.

00:02:02.657 --> 00:02:03.490
- I did not do this wisely.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.823
- You look so Spiderman-ish.

00:02:08.189 --> 00:02:10.439
(groaning)

00:02:14.927 --> 00:02:15.782
(laughter)

00:02:15.782 --> 00:02:17.976
- Okay you did that on purpose.

00:02:17.976 --> 00:02:19.550
You kicked me.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:22.450
(laughter)

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.740
- I knew I was gonna win.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:24.681
Yay!

00:02:24.681 --> 00:02:25.931
- [Leo] Oh god.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.833
- I don't know that we're gonna
be playing anymore Twister.

00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:31.710
(laughter)

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.253
We get very competitive with each other

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:35.484
and I think that was one
of the problems maybe.

00:02:35.484 --> 00:02:37.748
But I don't know it was kind of nice.

00:02:37.748 --> 00:02:39.365
I mean its...

00:02:39.365 --> 00:02:40.544
- Keeps you on your toes.

00:02:40.544 --> 00:02:42.892
- I think it's difficult,
you know, with relationships

00:02:42.892 --> 00:02:45.178
like how you move forward if you stay,

00:02:45.178 --> 00:02:48.359
if it can continue or
if it just breaks off.

00:02:48.359 --> 00:02:50.733
And so I don't know, for
me this confirmed that

00:02:50.733 --> 00:02:53.246
we still have good chemistry regardless of

00:02:53.246 --> 00:02:54.784
whatever happens in the future.

00:02:54.784 --> 00:02:57.648
- Like in the beginning
I felt some rigidness,

00:02:57.648 --> 00:03:00.908
you know it was awkward, with
the silence and everything.

00:03:00.908 --> 00:03:03.905
But as we got into the game,
something about the game,

00:03:03.905 --> 00:03:06.572
the atmosphere of a game at all,

00:03:07.638 --> 00:03:09.803
kind of lowered my guard a little bit.

00:03:09.803 --> 00:03:12.920
- I mean I'd like to think
that just being here today

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.886
and having this experience
could open the doors

00:03:16.886 --> 00:03:21.105
for us to just even talk
about it after this.

00:03:21.105 --> 00:03:22.656
- Congratulations for winning.

00:03:22.656 --> 00:03:23.489
- Oh thank you.

00:03:23.489 --> 00:03:24.920
(laughter)

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.420
(happy music)

